pitalized patients, where fluid balance can be disrupted. Additionally, the secretion of ADH is influenced by the body's fluid balance, further linking it to the onset of hyponatremia. Overall, ADH is a key hormone in the pathophysiology of hyponatremia, as its excessive secretion can result in significant alterations in sodium concentration due to increased water retention.\",78\r\n12951,ADH,SIADH,\"ADH, or antidiuretic hormone, is a hormone whose inappropriate secretion is responsible for the condition known as SIADH, or Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone secretion. SIADH is characterized by the excessive release of ADH, which results in water retention in the body. This condition can lead to hyponatremia, a potentially serious electrolyte imbalance caused by low sodium levels in the blood. Thus, the relationship between ADH and SIADH is crucial, as the dysregulation of ADH secretion directly contributes to the symptoms and complications associated with SIADH.\",74\r\n5343,DIETA,FÁRMACO,Diet can influence the absorption and effectiveness of various drugs,71\r\n11877,HIPÓFISIS,ADH,\"La hipófisis produce ADH, que es esencial para la regulación de la concentración urinaria y el equilibrio de líquidos en el cuerpo.\",68\r\n12998,SIADH,SRAA,The SRAA system is involved in the management of fluid balance in SIADH,66\r\n12956,HIPOFISITIS IGG4,SIADH,SIADH can be a complication following surgery related to conditions like hipofisitis IGG4,65\r\n12224,ACTH,ADH,\"ACTH influences the secretion of ADH, which can impact water balance and sodium levels\",34\r\n16111,RANDOMIZED CONTROLLED TRIAL,GASTRIC CANCER,Randomized controlled trials are used to evaluate the effectiveness of nutritional interventions in gastric cancer,27\r\n19842,SECRECIONES GASTROINTESTINALES,SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL AVANZADO,Secreciones gastrointestinales provide important electrolytes and minerals necessary for nutritional support,24\r\n15566,DIN,ORLISTAT,Orlistat can lead to nephrogenic diabetes ins